From: meanaverage <18336095+meanaverage@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 16:48:15 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 12/14] fix(web): keep clipboard monitoring and focus writes
 per component

The clipboard service stopped its monitoring loop through a module-level
`isComponentDestroyed` store, and queued clipboard writes that wait for window
focus in a module-level queue. With several components on a page, destroying
one stopped clipboard monitoring for all of them, and any focus event ran the
writes queued by every component.

Each ClipboardService now owns its monitoring timer and its pending focus
write (only the latest remote clipboard content is kept). Monitoring stops when
the session ends (the new `sessionEndedObservable`) and resumes with the next
session. A destroyed component disposes its clipboard service, cancels its
delayed resize, and does not dispatch `ready` if it was destroyed while
initializing. `shutdown()` forgets the session before shutting it down, so an
asynchronous clipboard read can't reach it afterwards.
